# wie_validate --keys: 배틀몬스터 (LGT) 새로하기 → 포획 튜토리얼 → 마을 → 집 안.
# Grammar and cap rule: `parse_keys` in wie_cli/src/bin/wie_validate.rs.
#
#   cargo run -q --release -p wie_cli --bin wie_validate -- --inject --boot-secs 6 \
#     --max-ticks 100000000000 --keys docs/keys/battlemonster-village.keys --shotdir <dir> <game>
#
# Step 95 (`95_OK`) is the village — reached 7/7 at load1 11-129 (docs/report/0298).
# Step 102 (`102_UP`) is inside the house only at low load (3/3 at <=55, 0/4 when
# load climbed to 65-129 on the last steps): a held key walks per tick, not per
# second, so the tail after the village is not load-proof. Target the village.
# The tutorial asks for STAR (43), CLR (47) and HASH (49) by name; its yes/no
# prompt (step 23) cannot be declined with NUM2. The gaps are wide on purpose:
# the fixed 27-key script feeds a 0.6 s grid, and under load the keys meant
# for later screens land on the help screen instead. Key names only — no game bytes.
# A script is tied to the engine it was recorded on: a fix that lets the game
# go further moves the path (the pre-#306 version of this path skipped the tutorial).
